From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:58:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(approval): the smart approval judge runs on the chat's
 API-key account

Both judge stages were configured on claude-pool, so a chat on an Anthropic API-key provider (claude-api-<account>) had its calls reviewed on the pool and got "all Claude accounts are at their limit" cards while it ran fine on its own key. A judge route that names claude-pool now runs on the reviewed chat's API-key provider with the configured judge model, using the rule 0147 gives subagents (a subagent follows its root chat; a scheduled run uses the job's own provider). A chat on the pool keeps the pool, and only when every pool account is at its limit or on hold do both stages move, for that review, to the API account with the most credit left: the estimate the hub shows (the plan's monthly credit less what Hermes spent through the key this cycle), read from the claude-accounts plugin loaded in the process. An account without credit or without a readable estimate is never chosen; with none, the user is asked as before. Any other chat and any judge route that does not name the pool are unchanged. The approval card names the API account that did the review, or that failed it.
